  "goodToKnow": "Die Kelle has several meanings: a ladle (die Schöpfkelle, die Suppenkelle), a bricklayer's trowel (die Maurerkelle), and the round red-and-white signalling disc that police and railway staff raise to stop traffic or signal departure (die Polizeikelle, die Signalkelle). Jemanden mit der Kelle rauswinken means a police officer waving you over. Plural: die Kellen."
